  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Among the following, the number of aromatic compound (s) is/are <br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/fyngifxripjhefbxvsdvsxxhqvgquhxobnwfnwhnswjfxjlenp.jpeg\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/29_solu_chem_pa1.jpg\"/></p><p>Cyclooctatetraene; <strong>non-aromatic</strong>, due to non-planarity of ring the <math><mi>π</mi></math>-electrons are not delocalised.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/29_solu_chem_pa1_2.jpg\"/></p><p>Cyclopropenyl anion; <strong>Anti-aromatic</strong>, <math><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi></math>-electrons are  delocalised</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/29_solu_chem_pa1_3.jpg\"/></p><p>Cyclopropenyl cation; <strong>Aromatic, </strong><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math>-electrons are  delocalised.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/29_solu_chem_pa1_4.jpg\"/></p><p>Cyclohexadiene : <strong>Non-aromatic, </strong>as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>π</mi></math> electrons are not fully conjugated.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/29_solu_chem_pa1_5.jpg\"/></p><p>Tropylium ion : <strong>Aromatic</strong>, as it contains conjugated system of  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> electrons (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math>electrons).  It is cyclic and planar.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/29_solu_chem_pa1_6.jpg\"/></p><p>Cyclopentadienyl cation; <strong>Anti-aromatic, </strong><math><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi></math>-electrons  are delocalised.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/29_solu_chem_pa1_7.jpg\"/></p><p>Cyclopentadienyl anion; <strong>Aromatic, </strong>as it contains conjugated system of  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> electrons (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> electrons).  It is cyclic and planar.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/29_solu_chem_pa1_8.jpg\"/></p><p>Both are aromatic as first it contains conjugated system of  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> electrons (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> electrons).  It is cyclic and planar. These are pi electrons present in one ring. Pi electrons present in other ring are not counted.</p><p>Second one contains conjugated system of  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> electrons (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math> electrons).  It is cyclic and planar. </p>",
    "image": null
  },
